  "prefLabel": "Plc 1603.04 Additional Attestation Required for Initial Registration Application",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1603.04 Additional Attestation Required for Initial Registration Application. In addition to the attestation required by Plc 304.05, the applicant’s signature shall constitute attestation that the applicant:\n\n(a) Has the financial resources to pay the nurses it places prior to receiving payment from the health care facility in which the nurses are placed; and\n\n(b) Understands and shall adhere to the obligations of RSA 326-M:3, namely:\n\n(1) Nurse agencies shall not commit the services of a single nurse or licensed nursing assistant to more than one health care facility for the same time period or shift and cancel a commitment to a facility, or compel that facility to bid again for services already promised it;\n\n(2) Nurse agencies shall not recruit potential employees on the premises of a health care facility;\n\n(3) Nurse agencies shall not charge a health care facility a higher amount based upon the presence in that facility of a communicable virus, except in the case of a state or local declaration of a public health emergency; and\n\n(4) Nurse agencies shall not facilitate the placement of any licensed professional with a license that is suspended.\n\nSource. #13914, eff 5-6-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1600.html"
}
